codex
The strongest new runtime candidate is in valley splitting: OpenMS reconstructs Savitzky–Golay coefficients for every parent trace. Caching the unchanged coefficients could remove substantial repeated work without changing the reduction order. I also confirmed that `all_out` → `PeakMap` moves spectrum payloads; transferring the whole vector should remove most of the 5-second assembly phase with a small change.
